00:37:56.610 --> 00:37:58.090
in having those two electrons.

00:37:58.090 --> 00:38:00.830
That's what a potential is.

00:38:00.830 --> 00:38:02.410
That's what a potential is.

00:38:02.410 --> 00:38:07.810
Oh, now so OK.

00:38:07.810 --> 00:38:09.710
Here we go.

00:38:09.710 --> 00:38:12.250
There's the volt. So what
determines it, right?

00:38:12.250 --> 00:38:16.010
What determines the potential?

00:38:16.010 --> 00:38:17.390
What determines the potential?

00:38:17.390 --> 00:38:18.680
Well, it's what I just said.

00:38:18.680 --> 00:38:21.590
You know, intuitively,
it's the difference

00:38:21.590 --> 00:38:23.190
in these things
wanting and saying,

00:38:23.190 --> 00:38:25.160
well, OK, I got copper and zinc.

00:38:25.160 --> 00:38:29.000
How do I know?

00:38:29.000 --> 00:38:33.050
Well, if you look at zinc--

00:38:33.050 --> 00:38:33.668
let me see.

00:38:33.668 --> 00:38:34.460
Where do I have it?

00:38:34.460 --> 00:38:35.120
Here we go.

00:38:35.120 --> 00:38:37.400
Zinc, I want to make
sure I get this right.

00:38:37.400 --> 00:38:48.090
So zinc is argon
and 3d10 and 4s2.

00:38:48.090 --> 00:38:51.800
All right, OK, copper, oh,
we got numbers 30 and 29.

00:38:51.800 --> 00:38:55.040
Copper is the same
thing in terms

00:38:55.040 --> 00:38:58.505
